{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011z5shUkibZ5E6d6W8eshkF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tNo declared condition was shown false in payload 8; no P0 found.\n2\t\n3\tNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n4\tNo P1 findings.\n5\t\n6\tP2 follow-ups\n7\t\n8\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_installer_write_safety/__init__.py:36\n9\tClass cloning preserves original bases: exported Incomplete no longer subclasses exported ParseError. Helpers such as parse_sed_script and _subst_commands therefore miss incomplete-fragment exceptions instead of returning their documented error/None result, potentially aborting the census without its report. Failure remains nonzero. Minimal fix: remap internal base classes through an original-to-clone map so Incomplete inherits the exported ParseError.\n10\t\n11\tP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_cost_transcripts_parts/__init__.py:55\n12\tRebinding generated dataclass __repr__ wrappers replaces their dataclasses globals with facade globals. On Python 3.9.6, repr(ScanCounters()) raises NameError for missing _thread; printing a transcript_rollup result also fails. Ordinary CLI rendering is unaffected. Minimal fix: rebind only methods whose actual __globals__ belongs to the declaration module; preserve external wrapper namespaces.\n13\t\n14\tValidation: 82 context-budget checks passed on Python 3.9.6; all 22 implementation files parsed successfully. The installer census completed over available files, but full baseline validation was limited by the withheld upgrade script.\n15\t\n16\tVERDICT: GO-WITH-CONDITIONS Two nonblocking compatibility regressions need follow-up, while this payload provides no evidence of a false declared condition or a P0 defect.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39b2a95c-7098-4a31-b7e8-36b062b92a5a","uuid":"d0c4590c-4925-44c1-b956-9d668914b49c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:25:27.871Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-re