{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011uTB2mKGCtYxzJB6TEvGjH","type":"tool_result","content":"455\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n456\t#\n457\t# The audit log is a GOVERNANCE ledger (agent_spawn rows; tokens_in/out on\n458\t# them are best-effort and frequently absent). The real token ledger is the\n459\t# harness-native transcript corpus — `message.usage` per assistant turn —\n460\t# which `.claude/scripts/ceo-cost-transcripts.py` reads with the full\n461\t# input / output / cache-read / cache-write-5m / cache-write-1h split and\n462\t# per-model prices. This module consumes that instrument through its\n463\t# programmatic API and prints BOTH sources, labelled, side by side.\n464\t# `--source audit` restores the pre-PLAN-186 rendering byte-for-byte.\n465\t#\n466\t# SCOPE NOTE (deliberate, not an oversight): this repo carries THREE\n467\t# independent pricing tables — `ceo-cost.py::_DEFAULT_PRICING`, the model\n468\t# registry behind `budget-summary.py::compute_cost_usd`, and the\n469\t# instrument's `_EMBEDDED_PRICING` / `cost-table.yaml` loader. Unifying them\n470\t# is a separate wave. This integration only REUSES what the instrument\n471\t# already exposes: the transcripts block is priced by the instrument, the\n472\t# audit block by whatever priced it before, and each block says so.\n473\t#\n474\t# The loader below is the one thing that cannot live in the instrument: its\n475\t# filename is hyphenated, so every caller needs its own importlib bootstrap.\n476\t# Everything else (root resolution, collection, rendering) is delegated, so\n477\t# the two callers cannot drift apart.\n478\t\n479\t_TRANSCRIPTS_MODULE_NAME = \"ceo_cost_transcripts\"\n480\t_TRANSCRIPTS_FILENAME = \"ceo-cost-transcripts.py\"\n481\t\n482\t\n483\tdef load_transcripts_instrument():\n484\t    \"\"\"Import `ceo-cost-transcripts.py` from next to this file, or None.\n485\t\n486\t    Fail-soft by construction: an 