tes the window (fails closed);\n  - census parse failures still block, except the carried Incomplete case below, which crashes with a nonzero exit.\n- Writes: context-budget and cost-transcripts stay read-only. The census --write-baseline path is unchanged.\n- Python: standard library only, plus _lib.runtime_paths and _lib.agent_frontmatter. Compatible with 3.9: I found no 3.10+ syntax or APIs.\n\nCARRIED (already declared, still present, not new)\n- P1, declared through lane notes claude-p08 and claude-p28. Location: .claude/hooks/_lib/_installer_write_safety/__init__.py:36.\n  - Cause: _bind_class clones Incomplete with its template base syntax.ParseError. In the entry point, issubclass(Incomplete, ParseError) is therefore False. The rebound `except ParseError` at commands.py:131 (in this payload; also in operands, model and verdicts_b) no longer catches the Incomplete that _read_balanced raises.\n  - Failure scenario: a scanned script with an unbalanced `${` on a sed side crashes the census (traceback, exit 1) instead of becoming an indeterminate site. CI still fails closed.\n  - Fix, as declared: remap __bases__ through the clones, or do not clone exception classes.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. The D2 removal note now gives a false governance claim. This sharpens the known rc1 stale-text P2.\n   - Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_context_budget_parts/status.py:97-102.\n   - What is wrong: --probe-status and --json emit \"non-canonical, no ceremony: the D2 block in this file\". The D2 block now lives in _lib/_context_budget_parts/summarization.py. That path matches the canonical guard \".claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py\" (canonical_edit/guards.py:34; `**` matches zero or more segments, paths.py:181-216). An in-session removal that follows the note is blocked by check_canonical_edit and needs a sentinel.\n   - The listed scope is also incomplete:\n     - status.py:14 imports ENV_SUMMARIZE_OLDEST from .summarization;\n     - context-budget.py:201 names \"summarization\" in its install tuple;\n     - so deleting the block as written breaks every context-budget.py run;\n     - MiddleOutPolicy (middle_out.py:137-140) uses _clamp_nonneg_int, which is defined in the D2 block. This coupling predates the split.\n   - Same false claim at summarization.py:20-21 and middle_out.py:22-23 (\"non-canonical and lives here in scripts/\").\n   - Fix: say \"canonical (_lib/**): sentinel required\" and list the real files: summarization.py, status.py:14 and the D2 record, and the context-budget.py install tuple and CLI flags. Move _clamp_nonneg_int out of the block first.\n\n2. Undeclared tightening of edit governance (new).\n   - What changed: the logic of context-budget.py, ceo-cost-transcripts.py and check-installer-write-safety.py moved from .claude/scripts/, which _CANONICAL_GUARDS does not list, into .claude/hooks/_lib/**, which it does.\n   - Effect on an adopter:\n     - CHANGELOG.md:37-39 and :122-123 say to re-apply a hand patch \"to the module\". That module now needs a sentinel ceremony that the original patch did not.\n     - Refreshing the embedded pricing table (_cost_transcripts_parts/pricing.py:21-30 and :52-55) is now a canonical edit. That table drives both the cost figures and the routing detector's alias vocabulary (routing_helpers.py:196).\n   - The entry points stay non-canonical, and an edit there can rebind any name after install(). So the guard adds friction without adding protection.\n   - Direction: closed. It blocks edits, never a session.\n   - Fix: add one CHANGELOG line saying that script logic moved into _lib is now under the canonical guard, or leave these non-governance packages outside the guard.\n\n3. Carried rc1 P2: dataclass repr() raises NameError.\n   - Where: _cost_transcripts_parts/__init__.py:54-56.\n   - Cause: the binder rebinds the dataclass __repr__ wrapper, because functools.wraps (reprlib on 3.13) stamps it with the template's __module__. In the entry point's globals, the wrapper's global _thread (get_ident on 3.13) no longer resolves.\n   - Effect: repr() of UsageRecord, ScanCounters, PricingResult and Priced raises NameError.\n   - No production path hits it: collect() returns JSON-safe data, and the `default=str` dumps at ceo-cost.py:768-772 never see a dataclass.\n   - Fix: rebind only functions whose __globals__ is the part module's dict.\n\n4. Carried rc1 P2s in the census package:\n   - _installer_write_safety/__init__.py:29-35 does not rebind property getters, so Site.blocking reads the template's BLOCKING_VERDICTS, not the entry point's.\n   - verdicts_b publishes _commands and _commands_name into the entry point.\n   - The fallback at engine.py:115, parents[3], is .claude, not the repo root.\n\n5. Stale location text (extends the known rc1 P2):\n   - ceo-cost-transcripts.py:32 says \"_EMBEDDED_PRICING below\", and :241-244 keeps a \"Pricing tables\" header over nothing.\n   - routing.py:307-321 ends with the ROOT_ENV doc comment that belongs to rollup.py:16.\n   - summarization.py:29 says the action names occur \"ONLY in this file\", but status.py:79-80 carries them too.\n   - docs/provider-pricing.md:152-153 sends a reader grepping ceo-cost-transcripts.py to a table that now lives in _lib/_cost_transcripts_parts/pricing.py:52.\n   - Fix: name the module paths.","decision":"GO","sentence":"This payload's 13 files match the rc1-reviewed blobs and make no declared condition false; I found no P0 and no new undeclared P1, since the one P1 still present (the census Incomplete/ParseError split) is already declared in the signed lane notes and everything else is P2 follow-up."},"ttft_ms":6965,"type":"result","duration_ms":621281,"uuid":"64499c04-1ea8-499d-ab0a-70e167034aa3","ttft_stream_ms":4606,"time_to_request_ms":177,"first_content_frame_ms":4606,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":86,"outputTokens":55244,"cacheReadInputTokens":7134054,"cacheCreationInputTokens":215